# 5. Requirement Example

## FR-001 — Register Prefund File

```text
Requirement ID: FR-001
Title: Register Prefund File
Type: FILE
Priority: P0
Status: REQUIRED

Business Objective:

Ensure every received prefund file is durably registered before
business transaction processing begins.

Actors:

External Payment Processing System
ACH Processing Platform

Trigger:

A new prefund file becomes available in the configured inbound
storage location.

Preconditions:

1. The file is available for reading.
2. The file is completely written.
3. The file has a valid file name.
4. The platform can access the configured storage.

Inputs:

1. File name
2. File size
3. File content
4. File checksum
5. Received timestamp

Processing:

1. Detect the file.
2. Verify that the file is complete.
3. Calculate the checksum.
4. Determine whether the file has already been registered.
5. Create a durable file registration record.
6. Assign a unique internal File ID.
7. Set the file state to REGISTERED.
8. Make the file eligible for processing.

Business Rules:

BR-001:
A file with the same business file identifier and checksum
shall not be processed more than once.

BR-002:
A file with the same business file identifier but a different
checksum shall be treated as a file integrity exception.

BR-003:
A file shall not enter transaction processing until registration
has been committed successfully.

Outputs:

File registration record.

State Changes:

RECEIVED → REGISTERED

Exceptions:

FILE_INCOMPLETE
FILE_DUPLICATE
FILE_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH
STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE
DATABASE_UNAVAILABLE

Retry Behavior:

STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE and DATABASE_UNAVAILABLE shall be retried
using the platform retry policy.

FILE_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH shall not be automatically retried.

Recovery Behavior:

If the application terminates after file registration but before
transaction processing, another application instance shall be able
to discover and continue processing the registered file.

Security Requirements:

The file shall be processed only by an authorized service identity.

Audit Requirements:

Record:

- File ID
- File name
- checksum
- received timestamp
- registration timestamp
- processing instance
- correlation ID

Observability Requirements:

Emit:

- file_registered event
- registration_success metric
- registration_failure metric
- correlation ID

Performance Requirements:

Registration shall not require loading the complete file into memory.

Dependencies:

Inbound file storage
Database

Acceptance Criteria:

AC-001:
Given a valid new prefund file,
when the file is detected,
then a REGISTERED record shall exist.

AC-002:
Given the same file is detected twice,
when the second detection occurs,
then the file shall not be processed twice.

AC-003:
Given database availability is lost,
when registration is attempted,
then the file shall remain available for later retry.

AC-004:
Given the application terminates after registration,
when another instance starts,
then the registered file shall be discoverable for processing.

AC-005:
Given a checksum mismatch,
when validation occurs,
then the file shall enter FILE_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH
and shall not be processed.

Test Scenarios:

TC-001 New valid file
TC-002 Duplicate file
TC-003 Same file ID with different checksum
TC-004 Database unavailable
TC-005 Application restart
TC-006 Concurrent processing by two pods
TC-007 Storage unavailable

Related Requirements:

FR-002
FR-003
BR-001
REC-001
```

This format gives an AI agent almost everything it needs to derive both **code and tests**.

