# 6. Business Rules

Business rules should have their own IDs.

Example:

```text
BR-001 — Duplicate Prefund File

Rule:

A prefund file shall not be processed more than once.

Uniqueness:

Business File ID + File Type

Exception:

If the same Business File ID exists with a different checksum,
the file shall be rejected as an integrity exception.

Expected State:

DUPLICATE_FILE

Expected Audit:

Record duplicate detection.

Test:

TC-BR-001
```

This is better than embedding a long paragraph inside another requirement.

---

# 7. State Transition Specification

Any workflow containing statuses should have an explicit state machine.

Example:

```text
Prefund File:

RECEIVED
   ↓
REGISTERED
   ↓
VALIDATING
   ↓
VALIDATED
   ↓
PROCESSING
   ↓
COMPLETED
```

Failure paths:

```text
VALIDATING → VALIDATION_FAILED

PROCESSING → PROCESSING_FAILED

PROCESSING → RETRY_PENDING
RETRY_PENDING → PROCESSING
```

For each transition specify:

```text
Current State:
Event:
Required Conditions:
Next State:
Failure State:
Can Retry:
Can Repeat:
Idempotent:
```

Example:

```text
Current State:
VALIDATED

Event:
START_PROCESSING

Conditions:
File validation completed successfully.

Next State:
PROCESSING

Failure:
PROCESSING_FAILED

Can Retry:
YES

Can Repeat:
NO

Idempotent:
YES
```

This is extremely useful for AI implementation because it prevents agents from inventing arbitrary state transitions.

