# 9. Exception Requirements

Do not bury exception behavior inside normal processing.

Create explicit requirements.

Example:

```text
REC-001 — Application Restart During Processing

Trigger:

Application instance terminates during transaction processing.

Expected Behavior:

1. In-progress work shall remain durably identifiable.
2. Another instance shall be able to discover incomplete work.
3. Previously completed transactions shall not be processed again.
4. Incomplete transactions shall resume or enter retry state.
5. Processing shall not create duplicate reservation requests.

Acceptance Criteria:

AC-REC-001:
Terminate the processing pod after database persistence and before
message publication.

Expected:

The transaction remains recoverable.

AC-REC-002:
Restart the application.

Expected:

The transaction is discovered and processing continues.

AC-REC-003:
Verify no duplicate business reservation occurs.
```

For enterprise platforms, these recovery requirements are as important as the happy path.

