# 24. AI-Friendly Writing Rules

When writing requirements for AI coding agents:

### Do

Use:

```text
shall
must
given
when
then
if
otherwise
only when
before
after
until
```

### Avoid

```text
etc.
and so on
as appropriate
if necessary
normally
typically
handle errors
process efficiently
support scalability
securely process
```

These words force the AI to guess.

---

# 25. Explicitly Define Ambiguity

If business behavior is unknown, write:

```text
OPEN-QUESTION-001

Question:
What should happen when settlement arrives before prefund
processing completes?

Options:

A. Reject settlement.
B. Hold settlement in WAITING_FOR_PREFUND.
C. Process settlement independently.

Decision:
B

Decision Owner:
Business

Decision Date:
YYYY-MM-DD
```

Never allow the AI agent to silently invent the answer.

---

# 26. Explicitly Define "Out of Scope"

This is extremely valuable.

Example:

```text
OUT-001

The platform shall not modify external IBM MQ infrastructure.

OUT-002

The platform shall not modify external payment processor systems.

OUT-003

The platform shall not perform settlement reconciliation against
systems not explicitly defined in this specification.
```

This prevents AI agents from expanding the implementation unnecessarily.

